---

The Swift provider creates SwiftPM applications and libraries with tools version 6.0. Follow [Your first Swift project](/docs/first-swift-project/) for a guided build and test.

## Generated package

| Component | Location and behavior |
| --- | --- |
| Core target | `Sources/<name>Core/Core.swift`; exports `sum` |
| Application | Optional `Sources/<name>/main.swift`; uses the core and prints `42` |
| Tests | `Tests/<name>Tests/CoreTests.swift`; XCTest checks addition and cancellation to zero |
| Manifest | `Package.swift`; declares products, targets, and their dependencies |

## Tasks

| Rivet task | Swift operation |
| --- | --- |
| Configure | `swift package describe` |
| Check / Build | `swift build` |
| Test | `swift test` |
| Run | `swift run` for the selected executable product |
| Format | `swift format format --in-place --recursive` over `Sources/` and `Tests/` |
| Lint | `swift format lint --strict --recursive` over `Sources/` and `Tests/` |
| Xcode | On macOS, open `Package.swift` in Xcode |

Build, Check, Test, and Run use the selected Debug/Release configuration. Format and Lint require a toolchain providing `swift format`. Compiler file/line diagnostics populate quickfix.

Executable discovery uses `swift package describe --type json`. SwiftPM can compile and evaluate `Package.swift` during discovery. See the [SwiftPM library workflow](https://www.swift.org/getting-started/library-swiftpm/) for native build and test commands.

## Source and target ownership

`:RivetFile` adds a source under a recorded target's conventional `Sources/<target>/` or `Tests/<target>/` directory. It preserves `Package.swift`. SwiftPM includes sources in those target directories; files placed elsewhere need corresponding native manifest configuration.

`:RivetTarget` adds an executable or library by regenerating `Package.swift`. It refuses a manifest edited outside Rivet. For a customized package, add products and targets directly in the manifest; native tasks discover them. [Swift package recovery](/docs/troubleshooting/#swift-package-customization) describes restoring a generated manifest when that is intentional.

Existing `Package.swift` projects work without `.rivet.json`. Dependencies, custom source paths, platform settings, and lockfiles remain under SwiftPM's control.

## Xcode integration

`:RivetTask xcode` opens the package on macOS. Apple application targets, signing, simulators, and SwiftUI previews belong in the Xcode application project. Rivet generates the Swift package only.
